I made a really cool discovery today.  :)
My character got his hands on a figurine of a succubus, and #applied it.
Actually, this was one of the best pets I've ever had, so much so that
a blessed figurine of a succubus is actually on my wish list.  (Pretty
far down the list, but still, it _is_ on there.)  Here's why...

*** Ward's Top Five Reasons to Have a Pet Succubus ***

5:  They are tough enough to stay around.  (That is, you won't lose her to
    a rock trap.)

4:  They don't eat corpses.  'nuff said.

3:  They are NOT tough enough to cause problems.  (They won't attack that
    friendly priest, for example.  They also won't kill _everything_ on a
    level before you can get XP for it, and they aren't a real threat if 
    they become unfriendly.

2:  They steal stuff from monsters they attack, just like nymphs do.  I had
    mine take a Wand of Fire right out of a gnome lord's hands and drop it
    at my feet.

1:  The discovery:  Headaches GO AWAY after a while!  The headache she gets
    after you've had your fun very obviously has a time out feature. 
    Furthermore, it is a FAST time out, only 100 turns or so!

One other thing I noticed...  I got a bad result the first two times, and then
she got a headache.  After the headache went away, the next _nine_ times (with
breaks every 2 or 3 times for headache time-outs) were all beneficial.
Practice makes perfect?  ;-)  Also, a tame succubus never charges you for 
"services rendered".  I guess it comes free with the "pet" status.  Needless 
to say, this has some serious potential for abuse.  Have fun...

...and, as always,
Happy Hacking.
